---
title: Numbering
order: 16
package: '@mdsvex/plugin-numbering'
example:
  source: |
    :::figure[Sales by month](id=fig:sales)
    A chart.
    :::

    Sales rose in March, as :ref[fig:sales] shows.
  with:
    - '@mdsvex/plugin-figures'
---
Numbers figures, tables, equations and sections, and turns `:ref[id]` into a link that reads as the number, in the way of [pandoc-crossref](https://lierdakil.github.io/pandoc-crossref/). The prefix of an id says what it is:

````svx
## Results

:::figure[Sales by month](id=fig:sales)
![A bar chart of sales by month](./sales.png)
:::

:::table[What each plan costs](id=tbl:plans)
| plan | price |
| --- | --- |
| free | 0 |
:::

```math id=eq:energy
E = mc^2
```

Sales rose in March (:ref[fig:sales]), the plans are in :ref[tbl:plans], :ref[eq:energy] gives the energy and :ref[sec:results] has the rest.
````

```html
<figure id="tbl:plans" class="table">
	<figcaption><span class="table-number">Table 1</span>: What each plan costs</figcaption>
	<table>...</table>
</figure>
<p>
	Sales rose in March (<span class="ref"><a href="#fig:sales">Figure 1</a></span>), the plans are in
	<span class="ref"><a href="#tbl:plans">Table 1</a></span>, <span class="ref"><a href="#eq:energy">Equation 1</a></span>
	gives the energy and <span class="ref"><a href="#results">Section 1</a></span> has the rest.
</p>
```

```ts
numbering({
	prefixes: { fig: ['Figure', 'Figures'], tbl, eq, sec }, // the word for one and for several, by kind
	and: 'and', // what joins the last two numbers
	number_sections: boolean = false, // the number in front of each heading
	section_depth: number = 2 // the depth of the headings numbered 1, 2, 3
});
```

- **`fig:`** is the `:::figure[Caption](id=fig:x)` of [`@mdsvex/plugin-figures`](/docs/plugins/figures), **`tbl:`** is `:::table[Caption](id=tbl:x)` around a table, **`eq:`** is a `math` fence with `id=eq:x` in its meta and **`sec:`** is a heading, `sec:` and its id. Each kind counts on its own, in document order.
- **A figure or table is numbered** when it has an id with its prefix, with a caption or without. The figures plugin owns the figure and renders its number, this plugin observes it.
- **An equation** gets its number as `\tag{n}`, which the [math renderer](/docs/reference/math) shows beside it, inside a `<div class="equation">` with its id.
- **`:ref[fig:a, fig:b]`** reads "Figures 1 and 2", the plural word, each number a link. A reference to an id that is not there is a warning and reads "Figure ?".
- **`prefix`** replaces the word: `:ref[fig:sales](prefix=Chart)` reads "Chart 1" and `prefix="Bar chart"` "Bar chart 1", the word as written, so a reference to several ids takes the plural. Only the literal `prefix=false` leaves the word out, "1" or "1 and 2". A capital for the start of a sentence is a word too, `prefix=Fig.` beside `prefixes: { fig: ['fig.', 'figs.'] }`.
- **Ids of different kinds** in one reference are a warning. It reads each kind with its own word, "Figure 1 and Table 1", and ignores a written `prefix`.
- **In a streaming view** a number is known when its target closes, and never changes. A reference to a target that has not arrived reads "Figure ?" until it does. Components read the numbers from [plugin data](/docs/plugins/writing/plugin-data), `plugin_data.numbering['target:' + id]`, through Svelte context.
